  "reviews": [
    {
      "name": "places/ChIJV_HlqXnzaS4R9iWXOROVGNY/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2paTVFrUTFWMWRQYTJGelJEaFZiM1I2YkZOSVRtYxAB",
      "relativePublishTimeDescription": "a year ago",
      "rating": 5,
      "text": {
        "text": "Dropped by **Woven Coffee** pretty last minute, and even though I didn’t get to try their coffee, I ended up enjoying their tea instead. Surprisingly, they have quite a nice variety of tea options, and the one I ordered was really enjoyable—simple but refreshing. It was actually a nice change of pace from the usual coffee stops.\n\nWhat makes Woven Coffee unique is that the stand is combined with a gurame bakar spot, so it kind of feels like you’re getting two vibes in one location. The interior itself is modest but fits the area well—cozy enough for a casual sit-down without trying too hard to be fancy. It works perfectly for a quick drink or a short catch-up with friends.\n\nIn terms of access, it’s quite practical. Parking is available for bikes, which is super handy if you’re just stopping by, and it’s also conveniently located near the Kampung Melayu halte, so it’s easy to reach with public transport. Another plus point is that they accept almost all payment methods, making things really hassle-free.\n\nOverall, Woven Coffee feels like a simple yet nice spot to grab tea or coffee when you’re around the area—casual, convenient, and easygoing.",
        "languageCode": "en"
      },
      "originalText": {
